Let me rewrite the parsing: match lines like `^'(.+)' depends on axioms: \[(.*)$` and continue on subsequent lines until `]`.
dsh: reasoning:
The multi-line continuation parsing is broken: when the axiom list is multi-line, the `while not body.endswith("]")` loop consumes the NEXT line via `next(it)` — but the outer `for line in lines` ALSO advances — double consumption, and when the multi-line case ends with a `]`-line, the loop logic mis-assigns (it took the next report line into body, leaving "]" never found → body grew into the next declaration's line). The result: some names got garbage axioms.

Fix the parsing robustly: iterate with an index or use a regex that handles multi-line via DOTALL:
```
pattern = re.compile(r"^'(.+)' depends on axioms: \[(.*?)\]\s*$", re.M | re.S)
for m in pattern.finditer(out):
    name = m.group(1).split(".")[-1]
    axs = set(x.strip() for x in m.group(2).split(",") if x.strip())
    reports[name] = axs
```
With re.M, ^$ match per line — but the body spans lines; use non-greedy .*? with re.S — but ^...$ with re.S + re.M: the $ matches before \n, so a multi-line body breaks. Use: `re.finditer(r"'(.+?)' depends on axioms: \[(.*?)\]", out, re.S)` — but that also matches the content between reports... Each report is `'Name' depends on axioms: [ ... ]` — non-greedy match: `'(.*?)' depends on axioms: \[(.*?)\]` with re.S — the name part: `'(.+?)'` — name contains quotes? The full name has no quotes ✓. This is robust.
